cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use WhatsApp Traceability Research Lab in research, please cite the software and the specific protocol papers reproduced in your work."
title: "WhatsApp Traceability Research Lab: Privacy-Preserving Traceability Research for Encrypted Messaging"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "WhatsApp Traceability Research Lab contributors"
version: 0.5.2
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/AmithKumar1/whatsapp-traceability-research
abstract: >-
  WhatsApp Traceability Research Lab is an alpha-stage research and evaluation framework for studying
  privacy-preserving source tracing in end-to-end encrypted messaging. It
  provides synthetic graph demonstrations, signed evidence manifests, a
  configurable multi-approver policy laboratory, an offline Merkle inclusion
  proof laboratory, synthetic path/tree research adapters, a shared benchmark
  harness, schemas, tests, and reproducibility documentation. The adapters are
  not yet interoperable reproductions of the referenced cryptographic protocols
  and do not integrate with WhatsApp.
